    "setting_description": "The tavern’s rectangular stone‑walled interior measures thirty feet east–west and forty feet north–south. A creaking wooden floor lies beneath, while a hearth along the west wall provides warmth; its chimney rises above it. North of the hearth runs a twenty‑foot counter parallel to the west wall, with barrels of ale lined every six feet. At the far eastern end of this counter sit four high bar stools, each topped by a crystal‑cup shelf.\n\nBehind the back door on the south wall stands a rectangular table, its front edge one foot from the wall. Two rows of round tables line both east and west sides: three along the west side at y = 10, 20, and 30 feet; three along the east side at the same north–south positions. Each round table has a small stool beside it.\n\nLanterns hang above every table—back and all six round tables—casting light that covers the entire tavern without overlap. The stone walls frame the space, their one‑foot thickness giving the room a sturdy medieval feel. All objects are positioned so none overlap; clear pathways lead from the back door to the central counter and around the tables.",
    "spatial_location_description": "The tavern occupies a rectangular interior of **30 ft east‑west (EW) by 40 ft north‑south (NS)** with stone walls that are **1 ft thick** on all sides.\n\n### Anchor objects\n1. **Back door** – Located at the south wall, centered **15 ft EW from the west corner**:  \n   - Width **2 ft**, height **7 ft**.  \n   - A wooden latch sits on its east side (west‑to‑east orientation).  \n   - The doorway opens toward the outside; no tables or counter occupy the 3 ft space between the door and the west wall.\n\n2. **Hearth / stone fireplace** – Along the west wall, centered northward:  \n   - Width **8 ft**, depth **6 ft** into the interior (extends from y = 16 to y = 22).  \n   - A chimney rises above it; a 4‑ft wide hearth counter sits just south of this fireplace.\n\n3. **Central counter** – Runs parallel to the west wall, positioned north of the hearth:  \n   - Length **20 ft EW**, width **4 ft NS** (from x = 5 to x = 25).  \n   - Counter edge is 2 ft south of the hearth’s front.  \n   - Barrels of ale line the counter, each barrel measuring **3 ft diameter × 4 ft tall**; they are spaced every 6 ft along the counter.\n\n### Additional furnishings\n- **High bar stools with crystal‑cup shelves** – Four stools sit at the eastern end of the counter (x = 20 to x = 24, y = 28).  \n  - Stools: height **4 ft**, seat width **2 ft × 2 ft**.  \n  - Shelves above each stool are **1 ft wide × 2 ft tall**.\n\n- **Back table** – A rectangular table behind the back door, centered at x = 15, y = 5:  \n  - Length **5 ft EW**, width **3 ft NS**.  \n  - Placed so that its front edge is 1 ft from the south wall.\n\n- **Round tables** – Six round tables are set throughout the interior:  \n  - Diameter **3 ft** each.  \n  - Two rows along the east and west walls, centered at y = 10, 20, and 30 respectively (x = 5 for west‑side tables; x = 25 for east‑side tables).  \n  - Each table has a small stool of its own: height **3 ft**, seat width **1.5 ft × 1.5 ft**.\n\n- **Lanterns** – A lantern hangs above every table (including the back table and each round table):  \n  - Lantern light radius **10 ft**, providing persistent illumination that covers the entire tavern without overlap.\n\nAll objects are positioned so none overlap: the counter sits neatly north of the hearth, the bar stools sit at the far eastern end of the counter with shelves above them, tables line both sides of the room leaving clear pathways to the back door and to the central counter. The stone walls frame the space, and the 1‑ft thick walls provide a sturdy medieval backdrop for this bustling tavern."
